I agree that for a fourth level character scrolls of enchant armor and
enchant weapon are a good choice; actually, the only types of scrolls that
you might not find enough of are identify, enchant armor/weapon, charging
and genocide, so you should choose among them. If you decide to go for 
enchanting, then what you should enchant depends of course on what you have.
If you already have a good weapon, then enchant it first (in Nethack, a good
weapon is much more valuable than good armor), otherwise enchant the piece of
armor that you would most likely keep later on (there is no purpose for
enchanting a cloak of invisibility for example, because sooner or later you
will find a stalker or a blessed potion of invisibility and you will leave the
cloak behind), ideally some of the really good armor pieces if you have any
(helm of telepathy, GDSM, Hawaiian shirt, speed / water walking boots,
gauntlets of dexterity, cloak of displacement, shield of reflection). Of
course, if the armor/weapon is not already rustproof, you should rustproof
it before enchanting it, to avoid duplicating the work.

However, I can't agree with what was said above about scrolls of genocide;
they are very useful, and you really need to genocide more than gelatinous
cubes and rust monsters. I always try to genocide most of the monsters in
the following list :

1. gelatinous cubes (can eat valuable organic objects; can paralyze you and
                     allow another monster to hack you to death).
2. liches (all three types; they can curse stuff you are wearing/carrying
           and there is no protection against that).
3. gremlins (can steal intrinsics from you, which can be fatal in Hell).
4. rust monsters (will eat metal and make your weapon/armor rust).
5. purple worms (you run the risk of being digested by them).
6. golden nagas (same problem as with liches, see above).
7. umber hulks (not really dangerous, but having the mazes totally dug up
                becomes very annoying).
8. cockatrices (you can be protected, but they always offer an opportunity
                for a stupid death).
9. rock moles (they eat metal).

In short, I try to be protected against instant deaths and extensive cursing
of items, which means that I always genocide types 1-3 before I enter Hell.

